# eBay Browse API credentials (Application access token / client-credentials
# grant — no per-user OAuth needed for search). Get these from
# https://developer.ebay.com/my/keys after creating a keyset. Copy this file
# to .env and fill in real values; .env is gitignored and never committed.
# EBAY_ENV selects which eBay host the client talks to: "sandbox" (fake test
# data, safe for development) or "production" (real listings). Start on
# sandbox until the scanning job is verified, then switch to production.
EBAY_ENV=sandbox
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# AI part identification (the "Identify Parts" button on a Listing). The
# backend shells out to the `omp` CLI, which must be installed and on PATH.
# Both variables below are OPTIONAL and empty by default: with neither set,
# omp uses its own default model and the host's already-logged-in session, so
# no API key is required for local development. Set AI_IDENTIFY_MODEL to pin a
# specific model (passed through as `--model=<value>`), and AI_IDENTIFY_API_KEY
# to authenticate with a real API key instead of the logged-in session
# (passed through as `--api-key=<value>`) — e.g. for a deployment with no
# interactive login, the same way EBAY_CLIENT_ID/EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET work.
AI_IDENTIFY_MODEL=
AI_IDENTIFY_API_KEY=
